    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for Ghost Ride the WHIP hinges on capitalizing on several high-upside matchups against mediocre arms. **Tyler Soderstrom** leads the charge with an elite 72.71 score, benefiting from an advantageous combination of a hitters' park and a favorable matchup against Mitch Keller. Similarly, **Josh Naylor** (71.15) and **James Wood** (71.10) are locked in as primary assets; **James Wood** remains a vital engine for our roster, as his elite .407 xwOBA and stolen base upside help maintain our categorical edge even when facing a solid veteran like Wacha. **Seiya Suzuki** also presents a strong play (68.63) by capitalizing on the favorable park factors and the 4.69 xERA of Feltner, solidifying the heart of our lineup.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Alex Freeland**, who fell just short of the cut at 36.56. While **Alex Freeland** offers switch-hitting versatility, his projected #9 spot in the order significantly suppressed his efficiency score compared to the aggressive placement of **Cole Young** or **Brice Turang**. We are exercising caution with **Corbin Carroll** (51.08) and **Gabriel Moreno** (43.71), as both face Reid Detmers; while Detmers is a formidable lefty, the projected order placement for **Corbin Carroll** keeps him in the mix, though his stolen base potential is slightly dampened by the presence of a high-efficiency defensive catcher.\n\nRisks remain throughout the board as several lineups are still pending, forcing us to rely on historical batting order assumptions for players like **Dalton Rushing** and **Jose Caballero**. The platoon disadvantage for **Travis Bazzana** (48.67) against Robert Gasser makes him our most vulnerable start, and while he is currently in the UTIL slot, we will monitor pre-game lineups closely to ensure our active roster isn't compromised by unexpected benchings. With **Mickey Moniak** and **Trevor Story** still on the shelf, our bench depth is thin; we are relying on **Zach McKinstry** to stay ready should we need to pivot late in the day due to weather or last-minute lineup adjustments.",
